 245:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c **** /*
 246:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * Maximum number of "basic operations" to be done in a row.
 247:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *
 248:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * Default value 0 means that ECC operations will not yield.
 249:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * Note that regardless of the value of ecp_max_ops, always at
 250:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * least one step is performed before yielding.
 251:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  *
 252:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * Setting ecp_max_ops=1 can be suitable for testing purposes
 253:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  * as it will interrupt computation at all possible points.
 254:Libs/mbedtls/library/ecp.c ****  */
